                <pb facs="0255" n="139" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg139"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.51/947.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of Conversation between the Chinese Minister
                        and the Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-06-16">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 16, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Mr. Chang was told that the Department had again cabled the representatives of
                    the American financial group at Paris urging prompt action be taken in the
                    matter of advances as requested by the Chinese Government. It was also pointed
                    out that while in this respect we had done all that was possible, nevertheless,
                    owing to difference in time, the Chinese Government on its part ought to be
                    prepared for a delay of two or three days, inasmuch as even under the most
                    favorable circumstances the matter would obviously require some little time.</p>
            </div>
